en=efa5b863&mode=fill&top=57&left=0&width=600&height=200&format=webp\",\"w1200\":\"https://d117kfg112vbe4.cloudfront.net/public/Royal-Albert-Hall-DAMS/Promoter-Imagery/2026/7-July/BBC-Proms-2026/Prom-17-Elgars-First-2820-x-1480-JUL-29.jpg?type=image&id=7171&token=efa5b863&mode=fill&top=114&left=0&width=1200&height=400&format=webp\",\"alt\":\"Claire Booth\",\"caption\":\"Claire Booth © Sven Arnstein \"},\"Performances\":[{\"ID\":\"2081-101162\",\"PerformanceNumber\":101162,\"ProductionSeasonNumber\":99706,\"Date\":\"2026-07-29T19:00:00+01:00\",\"TimeSlot\":\"Evening\",\"HasTicketsUnderX\":true,\"OnSaleDate\":\"2026-05-16T09:00:00+01:00\",\"OffSaleDate\":\"2026-07-29T18:25:00+01:00\",\"MinimumPrice\":5.1,\"MaximumPrice\":46,\"WebContents\":[{\"ContentTypeId\":1,\"ContentType\":\"Web SYOS\",\"Content\":\"yes\",\"Inactive\":false},{\"ContentTypeId\":10,\"ContentType\":\"Web Max Quantity Performance\",\"Content\":\"12\",\"Inactive\":false},{\"ContentTypeId\":54,\"ContentType\":\"Proms Thumbnail url\",\"Content\":\"https://d117kfg112vbe4.cloudfront.net/public/Royal-Albert-Hall-DAMS/Promoter-Imagery/2026/7-July/BBC-Proms-2026/Prom-17-Elgars-First-2820-x-1480-JUL-29.jpg?type=image&id=7171&token=efa5b863\",\"Inactive\":false},{\"ContentTypeId\":66,\"ContentType\":\"Members - Web Description\",\"Content\":\"<div>\\r\\n<div>\\r\\n<div>\\r\\n<p>&lsquo;Human life &hellip; and a massive hope in the future&rsquo;: this &ndash; no less &ndash; is&nbsp;<strong>Elgar</strong>&rsquo;s sweeping subject for his&nbsp;<em>First Symphony</em>&nbsp;&ndash; a work once nicknamed &lsquo;Brahms&rsquo;s Fifth&rsquo; for its close relationship with the German tradition. Exuberant and filled with orchestral colour, an &lsquo;immediate and phenomenal success&rsquo; at its premiere, it&rsquo;s the work of a composer steeped in musical history but looking to the future.</p>\\r\\n<p>Two contemporary works open this concert by&nbsp;<strong>Ryan Wigglesworth</strong>&nbsp;and the&nbsp;<strong>BBC Scottish Symphony Orchestra</strong>: the world premiere of&nbsp;<em>The World&rsquo;s Wife</em>&nbsp;by&nbsp;<strong>Brett Dean</strong>&nbsp;&ndash; setting words by&nbsp;<strong>Carol Ann Duffy</strong>&nbsp;&ndash; and&nbsp;<strong>Judith Weir</strong>&rsquo;s&nbsp;<em>Moon and Star</em>&nbsp;&ndash; capturing the vastness and strangeness of space through the eyes of New England poet&nbsp;<strong>Emily Dickinson</strong>.</p>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n<section>\\r\\n<div>\\r\\n<h2>Programme</h2>\\r\\n<div>\\r\\n<div>\\r\\n<div>\\r\\n<p><strong>Judith Weir&nbsp;</strong>Moon and Star&nbsp;<em>15&rsquo;</em>&nbsp;<br /><strong>Brett Dean</strong>&nbsp;The World&rsquo;s Wife&nbsp;<em>c20&rsquo;&nbsp;</em><br /><em>BBC co-commission: world premiere</em></p>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n<div>\\r\\n<div>Interval<hr /></div>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n<div>\\r\\n<div>\\r\\n<p><strong>Elgar</strong>&nbsp;Symphony No. 1 in A flat major&nbsp;<em>50&rsquo;</em></p>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n<div>\\r\\n<p><strong>Claire Booth&nbsp;</strong><em>soprano</em></p>\\r\\n<p><strong>BBC Singers</strong><br /><strong>BBC Scottish Symphony Orchestra&nbsp;</strong><br /><strong>Ryan Wiggleswort</strong>h&nbsp;<em>conductor&nbsp;</em></p>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n</section>\",\"Inactive\":false},{\"ContentTypeId\":228,\"ContentType\":\"PT: 18 & Under\",\"Content\":\"The government have introduced a temporary reduced rate of VAT for children's tickets of 5% between 25 June and 1 September, and the prices of BBC Proms 18-and-under tickets for this period have been reduced in order to pass this reduced rate onto customers.\",\"Inactive\":false}]}]},{\"ID\":2130,\"ProductionSeasonNumber\":99706,\"PerformanceNumber\":101111,\"WishlistNumber\":447,\"StartDate\":\"2026-08-31T19:00:00+01:00\",\"EndDate\":\"2026-08-31T19:00:00+01:00\",\"Prefix\":\"BBC Proms presents\",\"Title\":\"BBC Proms: Enchanted - Alan Menken’s Music for Disney\",\"Suffix\":null,\"ListingIndicator\":nul