uo;s hard-won&nbsp;<em>Symphony No. 2</em>&nbsp;&ndash; a profoundly personal triumph forged in the failure of his First Symphony over a decade earlier &ndash; is the centrepiece of this concert by Manchester&rsquo;s&nbsp;<strong>Hall&eacute; orchestra</strong>&nbsp;and its Principal Conductor&nbsp;<strong>Kahchun Wong</strong>. Its expansive, late-Romantic lyricism meets the glowing, pealing soundscape of&nbsp;<strong>Ravel</strong>&rsquo;s &lsquo;<em>The Valley of the Bells</em>&rsquo; from his Miroirs, orchestrated by&nbsp;<strong>Colin Matthews</strong>.</p>\\r\\n<p>Pianist<strong>&nbsp;Alexandra Dariescu</strong>&nbsp;makes her Proms debut in&nbsp;<strong>Nadia Boulanger</strong>&rsquo;s boldly poetic 1912&nbsp;<em>Fantasy for piano and orchestra</em>, with its eclectic nods to Franck, Faur&eacute; and Stravinsky.</p>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n<section>\\r\\n<div>\\r\\n<h2>Programme</h2>\\r\\n<div>\\r\\n<div>\\r\\n<div>\\r\\n<p><strong>Ravel, orch. Colin Matthews</strong>&nbsp;La vall&eacute;e des cloches&nbsp;<em>6&rsquo;&nbsp;</em><br /><strong>N. Boulanger</strong>&nbsp;Fantasy for piano and orchestra&nbsp;<em>20&rsquo;</em>&nbsp;</p>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n<div>\\r\\n<div>Interval<hr /></div>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n<div>\\r\\n<div>\\r\\n<p><strong>Rachmaninov</strong>&nbsp;Symphony No. 2 in E minor&nbsp;<em>60&rsquo;</em></p>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n<div>\\r\\n<p><strong>Alexandra Dariescu&nbsp;</strong><em>piano</em></p>\\r\\n<p><strong>Hall&eacute;&nbsp;</strong><br /><strong>Kahchun Wong</strong>&nbsp;<em>conductor&nbsp;</em></p>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n</section>\",\"Inactive\":false},{\"ContentTypeId\":228,\"ContentType\":\"PT: 18 & Under\",\"Content\":\"The government have introduced a temporary reduced rate of VAT for children's tickets of 5% between 25 June and 1 September, and the prices of BBC Proms 18-and-under tickets for this period have been reduced in order to pass this reduced rate onto customers.\",\"Ina