Albert-Hall-DAMS/Promoter-Imagery/2026/7-July/BBC-Proms-2026/Horrible-Sciences-2820x1487-v3.png?type=image&id=7678&token=cb00ab16&mode=fill&top=0&left=11&width=410&height=228&format=webp\",\"w820\":\"https://d117kfg112vbe4.cloudfront.net/public/Royal-Albert-Hall-DAMS/Promoter-Imagery/2026/7-July/BBC-Proms-2026/Horrible-Sciences-2820x1487-v3.png?type=image&id=7678&token=cb00ab16&mode=fill&top=0&left=22&width=820&height=456&format=webp\",\"w600\":\"https://d117kfg112vbe4.cloudfront.net/public/Royal-Albert-Hall-DAMS/Promoter-Imagery/2026/7-July/BBC-Proms-2026/Horrible-Sciences-2820x1487-v3.png?type=image&id=7678&token=cb00ab16&mode=fill&top=58&left=0&width=600&height=200&format=webp\",\"w1200\":\"https://d117kfg112vbe4.cloudfront.net/public/Royal-Albert-Hall-DAMS/Promoter-Imagery/2026/7-July/BBC-Proms-2026/Horrible-Sciences-2820x1487-v3.png?type=image&id=7678&token=cb00ab16&mode=fill&top=116&left=0&width=1200&height=400&format=webp\",\"alt\":null,\"caption\":null},\"Performances\":[{\"ID\":\"2075-101160\",\"PerformanceNumber\":101160,\"ProductionSeasonNumber\":99706,\"Date\":\"2026-07-25T18:00:00+01:00\",\"TimeSlot\":\"Evening\",\"HasTicketsUnderX\":true,\"OnSaleDate\":\"2026-05-15T09:00:00+01:00\",\"OffSaleDate\":\"2026-07-25T17:25:00+01:00\",\"MinimumPrice\":5.1,\"MaximumPrice\":46,\"WebContents\":[{\"ContentTypeId\":1,\"ContentType\":\"Web SYOS\",\"Content\":\"yes\",\"Inactive\":false},{\"ContentTypeId\":10,\"ContentType\":\"Web Max Quantity Performance\",\"Content\":\"12\",\"Inactive\":false},{\"ContentTypeId\":66,\"ContentType\":\"Members - Web Description\",\"Content\":\"<div>\\r\\n<div>\\r\\n<div>\\r\\n<p>Join Albert Einstein and Marie Curie as they share the DNA of CBBC&rsquo;s hit comedy sketch show&nbsp;<strong>Horrible Science</strong>&nbsp;live at the Royal Albert Hall with some scientifically proven bangers from the classical canon.</p>\\r\\n<p>They&rsquo;ll be joined by some of the great characters from science to introduce sensational sounds from&nbsp;<strong>Holst</strong>&rsquo;s&nbsp;<em>The Planets</em>&nbsp;to&nbsp;<strong>John Williams</strong>&rsquo;s&nbsp;<em>Star Wars</em>. But will the Prom survive Dr Big Brain&rsquo;s devilish desire to conquer the universe?&nbsp;</p>\\r\\n<p><em>Relaxed performance</em><br /><em>Broadcast on BBC TV and BBC iPlayer&nbsp;</em></p>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n<section>\\r\\n<div>\\r\\n<h2>Programme</h2>\\r\\n<div>\\r\\n<div>\\r\\n<div>Excerpts from:</div>\\r\\n<div>\\r\\n<p><strong>Borodin</strong>&nbsp;Prince Igor &ndash; Polovtsian Dances&nbsp;<br /><strong>G. Holst&nbsp;</strong>The Planets<br /><strong>John Williams</strong>&nbsp;Star Wars</p>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n<div>\\r\\n<p><strong>Richard David Caine</strong><br /><strong>James McNicholas</strong><br /><strong>Jessica Ransom</strong><br /><strong>Inel Tomlinson</strong></p>\\r\\n<p><strong>BBC National Orchestra of Wales&nbsp;</strong><br /><strong>Karen N&iacute; Bhroin</strong>&nbsp;<em>conductor&nbsp;</em></p>\\r\\n<p><em>There will be one interval.</em></p>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n</div>\\r\\n</section>\",\"Inactive\":false},{\"ContentTypeId\":228,\"ContentType\":\"PT: 18 & Under\",\"Content\":\"The government have introduced a temporary reduced rate of VAT for children's tickets of 5% between 25 June and 1 September, and the prices of BBC Proms 18-and-under tickets for this period have been reduced in order to pass this reduced rate onto customers.\",\"Inactive\":false}]}]},{\"ID\":2174,\"ProductionSeasonNumber\":101968,\"PerformanceNumber\":101969,\"WishlistNumber\":null,\"StartDate\":\"2026-10-17T21:30:00+01:00\",\"EndDate\":\"2026-10-17T21:30:00+01:00\",\"Prefix\":\"Royal Albert Hall presents\",\"Title\":\"David Moore\",\"Suffix\":null,\"ListingIndicator\":null,\"Summary\":\"Contemporary composer David Moore performs music from his critically acclaimed solo piano album Graze the Bell.\",\"Image\":{\"w300\":\"https://d117kfg112vbe4.cloudfront.net/public/Royal-Albert-Hall-DAMS/Promo